WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.960
Kicking off the week on Tesla's short time,

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:05.660
daily, episode 511, I'm Patrick and Vancouver.

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:08.620
Today is June 15th, 2026.

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:11.560
Here's what's kicking off the week in Tesla land.

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:14.720
ABF freight's order of two Tesla semis

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:17.360
puts the first long-range electric trucks

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:19.280
into California line haul service

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:21.280
with routes extending to Reno.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:25.000
European regulators are questioning the safety data

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.720
Tesla submitted for full self-driving approvals.

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:31.700
Reuters and investigators flagged overstated collision

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:34.200
and intervention rates in the filings used

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.460
for EU approvals.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:38.480
Multiple national regulators have paused

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:41.220
or reexamined the submissions as a result.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:45.040
Tesla has not responded publicly to the specific claims.

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:47.920
The issue adds documentation overhead

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:51.120
and potential delays to the staggered European rollout.

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:55.520
Regulators evaluating supervised driver assistance systems

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:57.280
face a basic measurement problem.

00:00:57.860 --> 00:00:59.800
The data they receive must reflect

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:02.640
the same operating conditions the public will encounter.

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:07.440
Tesla's European submissions reportedly mixed supervised miles

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:10.280
with claims that implied lower intervention rates

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:11.920
than the raw logs supported.

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:16.080
When the gap surfaced, several national authorities paused

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:18.520
further review rather than risk approving

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:19.740
on incomplete evidence.

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:23.620
The practical consequence is that every additional supervised

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:26.660
mile now carries extra documentation overhead.

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:29.640
Tesla must either narrow the data set

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:33.160
to only the cleanest segments or accept longer approval windows

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:35.660
while it rebuilds the underlying safety case.

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:38.520
Either path raises the cost of scaling

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:40.260
the same software across borders.

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:43.500
It is a function of traceable, auditable miles.

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:46.840
Until the submission process itself is standardized,

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.960
each new market adds a fixed compliance layer

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:51.960
that competes with the marginal revenue

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:53.420
from software subscriptions.

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:57.240
Starlink ran advertisements during the UFC Freedom

00:01:57.240 --> 00:01:59.660
250 event on Paramount Plus.

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:02.440
The placement puts the satellite service

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:04.700
in front of a large live sports audience.

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:08.660
Tesla and SpaceX share overlapping brand exposure

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:09.500
through this channel.

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:13.900
The ad run comes as SpaceX continues scaling its user base.

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:16.800
Viewers will see whether similar placements expand

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:18.700
into other major broadcasts.

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:21.760
Wedbush analyst Dan Ives released a note

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:24.460
analyzing SpaceX's IPO effects.

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:28.040
He described the debut pricing as a goldilocks outcome

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:31.180
that avoided draining capital from the broader tech trade.

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:34.840
Ives highlighted continued AI infrastructure spending

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:37.840
and named Palantir, Snowflake, and DataDog

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:39.500
as data layer beneficiaries.

00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:43.140
The note also flagged hyperscaler cloud growth

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:44.600
at Microsoft and Amazon.

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:48.100
Investors will track whether the same capital

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:51.640
rotation dynamic appears in Tesla's own valuation multiples.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:55.500
Tesla shares Rose alongside broader market reaction

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:57.360
to the US-Iran peace agreement.

00:02:58.020 --> 00:03:01.560
The move added roughly 1.5% to the stock on the day.

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:05.160
Analyst attributed the gain to macro sentiment

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:07.520
rather than any new EV demand signal.

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:11.020
The price action shows how geopolitical headlines

00:03:11.020 --> 00:03:14.420
can still move the name even when fundamentals remain unchanged.

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:17.880
Next earnings release will separate sentiment effects

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:19.280
from delivery trends.

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:21.660
While approval friction builds in Europe,

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:24.060
Tesla is seeing concrete commercial traction

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:26.000
for another vehicle in North America.

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:29.200
ABF freight purchased two Tesla semis

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:30.840
to support its fleet operations.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:34.740
The trucks will handle line haul runs inside California

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:38.120
and extend into Reno, Nevada, and additional locations.

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:41.760
This marks one of the first documented fleet purchases

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:44.240
for the semi in active commercial service.

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:47.140
The move tests real world economics

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:49.700
on routes that makes highway and regional miles.

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:53.340
Next data point to watch is any follow on orders

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:56.600
or performance metrics ABF shares after deployment.

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:58.940
From trucks already hitting the road,

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:00.880
we turned to a new passenger model

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:03.460
now reaching customers on the other side of the world.

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:07.800
Tesla started delivering the six seat model YL in India

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:11.140
at a starting price of approximately 62 lock rupees.

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:15.100
The vehicle targets buyers seeking larger family configurations

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:16.680
in the premium segment.

00:04:17.300 --> 00:04:19.920
Initial units are reaching customers in major cities.

00:04:20.420 --> 00:04:22.320
The launch extends Tesla's footprint

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:24.980
beyond the standard model Y already on sale.

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:27.960
Sales figures from the first quarter of deliveries

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:29.800
will show whether the longer wheel base

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:31.060
vary in gains traction.

00:04:31.860 --> 00:04:34.160
Stronger demand signals are also appearing

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:36.120
in Tesla's largest single market.

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:39.880
Tesla China posted its strongest month of 2026

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:42.820
with nearly 86,000 units in May.

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:45.940
Volume rose 39% year over year

00:04:45.940 --> 00:04:49.300
and approaches a 1 million unit annualized run rate.

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:53.820
European sales through May ran roughly 95,000 units

00:04:53.820 --> 00:04:55.300
ahead of the prior year.

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:59.440
Q2 deliveries are tracking approximately 28% higher

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:00.220
than last year.

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:03.080
Volume growth at existing factories

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:05.940
pairs with new capacity coming online elsewhere.

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:10.500
First structural beams went up at the 5.2 million square foot

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:13.220
Optimus Gigatex's North Campus site.

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:17.420
The long-term output target remains 10 million units per year.

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:20.620
The low volume production timing is still listed

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:22.760
as summer 2026 or later.

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:27.520
The AI-5 chip is slated to debut on Optimus before vehicles.

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:30.220
Energy storage is also scaling up

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:31.880
with a new dedicated factory.

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:36.120
Exterior construction is complete at the Houston Megapack plant

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:38.700
that reached a $200 million investment.

00:05:39.460 --> 00:05:41.800
Production is slated for late 2026.

00:05:42.220 --> 00:05:44.540
Combined with Lathrop and Gigashanghai,

00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:49.180
total Megapack capacity will exceed 130 gigawatt hours

00:05:49.180 --> 00:05:49.880
per year.

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:54.200
The new Megablock unit packs 20 Megawatt hours AC

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:57.140
and claims 40% lower construction cost.

00:05:57.800 --> 00:06:00.460
Researchers tested new sodium ion cells

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:02.620
that reach full charge in 15 minutes

00:06:03.180 --> 00:06:05.980
while matching energy density of some current Tesla packs.

00:06:06.860 --> 00:06:10.280
The chemistry avoids lithium and cobalt supply constraints.

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:14.080
Performance held steady across multiple fast charge cycles

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:15.160
in lab conditions.

00:06:15.820 --> 00:06:17.820
The results add another potential path

00:06:17.820 --> 00:06:19.780
for lower cost battery production.

00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:23.280
Tesla's own cell development teams will monitor

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:26.360
whether sodium ion reaches automotive grade durability.

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:30.300
Elon Musk's stated SpaceX could reach $1 trillion

00:06:30.900 --> 00:06:32.780
in annual revenue by 2030.

00:06:33.520 --> 00:06:35.920
The projection follows the company's first trading

00:06:35.920 --> 00:06:37.280
day after its IPO.

00:06:37.820 --> 00:06:41.040
SpaceX closed that session at a roughly $2.1 trillion

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:42.660
market capitalization.

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:46.120
The revenue target assumes continued Starlink growth

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:47.480
and new launch contracts.

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:51.020
Tesla investors will watch how the two companies' capital

00:06:51.020 --> 00:06:53.320
needs interact over the next four years.

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:55.680
While hardware capacity grows,

00:06:56.240 --> 00:06:59.140
software updates continue to iterate on autonomy features.

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:03.960
The latest supervised FSD build includes onscreen messages

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:07.080
such as vehicle will pull over near destination.

00:07:07.640 --> 00:07:10.920
Reviewers logged 250 miles and called the version

00:07:10.920 --> 00:07:14.420
the strongest iteration yet for natural obstacle avoidance.

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:17.840
The release cadence has compressed to roughly every two

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:18.460
to three weeks.

00:07:18.860 --> 00:07:21.480
The same autonomy effort now has a published playbook

00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:22.940
for emergency situations.

00:07:23.860 --> 00:07:26.600
Tesla published a first responder interaction plan

00:07:26.600 --> 00:07:29.240
outlining procedures for police stops, collisions,

00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:30.260
and severe weather.

00:07:31.140 --> 00:07:35.180
The document covers SAE level four operation protocols.

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:38.000
It details how the vehicle will communicate

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:41.440
with emergency personnel and when it will yield control.

00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:44.940
The plan is required for regulatory filings

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:46.260
in multiple jurisdictions.

00:07:47.080 --> 00:07:49.940
On the competitive front, another company is delivering

00:07:49.940 --> 00:07:52.540
something Tesla once discussed but never shipped.

00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:55.320
Xiaomi introduced a portable charger

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:58.080
that can top up in EV even when the owner is away

00:07:58.080 --> 00:07:58.800
from the vehicle.

00:07:59.720 --> 00:08:02.980
The device addresses a use case Tesla discussed years earlier

00:08:02.980 --> 00:08:04.320
but never brought to market.

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:08.460
Xiaomi's version integrates with its own vehicle app ecosystem.

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:11.840
The product highlights how competitors are filling gaps

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:13.320
in the charging experience.

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:16.320
broader policy moves could also shape

00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:18.640
where Chinese-made Teslas can be sold.

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:22.200
Canadian officials are evaluating import quotas

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:23.960
on Chinese-made electric vehicles.

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:28.180
The discussion follows a reported 40% rise in exports

00:08:28.180 --> 00:08:32.180
from Chinese manufacturers including BYD and Tesla's Shanghai

00:08:32.180 --> 00:08:32.780
plant.

00:08:33.540 --> 00:08:37.140
Tesla vehicles built in China would fall under any new limits.

00:08:37.580 --> 00:08:39.960
The policy shift could affect pricing and availability

00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:41.340
for Canadian buyers.

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:44.000
Industry groups are preparing submissions

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:46.100
ahead of any formal rulemaking.

00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:49.520
Tomorrow we'll be watching for any public clarification

00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:52.900
from Tesla on the European FSD data questions

00:08:53.580 --> 00:08:56.860
and the first performance metrics from ABF freight semi-roots.

00:08:57.820 --> 00:08:59.860
That covers it for today's Tesla developments.

